\[ \hat{\sigma}(a(x_1 - x_2)) = \frac{1}{n} \sum_{i=1}^{n} (x_i - \mu_i)^2 \]

Substituting \( n = 2 \):
\[ \hat{\sigma}(a(x_1 - x_2)) = \frac{1}{2} \left( \sum_{i=1}^{2} (x_i - \mu_i)^2 \right) \]

**Expressing \( \hat{\sigma}(a(x_1 - x_2)) \)**:
\[ \hat{\sigma}(a(x_1 - x_2)) = \frac{1}{2} \left[ \sum_{i=1}^{2} (x_i - \mu_i)^2 + \frac{1}{2} \left( \mu_i - \hat{\sigma}(a(x_1 - x_2)) \right)^2 \right] \]

**Simplify the expression:**
\[ \hat{\sigma}(a(x_1 - x_2)) = \frac{1}{2} \left( \sum_{i=1}^{2} (x_i - \mu_i)^2 + \frac{(a(x_1 - x_2))^2}{4} \right) \]

**Summarize the summands:**
\[ \hat{\sigma}(a(x_1 - x_2)) = \frac{1}{2} \left( \sum_{i=1}^{2} (x_i - \mu_i)^2 + \frac{a^2(x_1 - x_2)}{4} \right) \]

