\[ a = \frac{1}{2} \left( \sum_{i=1}^{2} (x_i - \mu_i)^2 + \frac{a^2(x_1 - x_2)}{4} \right) \]

**Calculate the sums:**
\[ \sum_{i=1}^{2} (x_i - \mu_i)^2 = \frac{1}{2} \left( \sum_{i=1}^{2} (x_i - \mu_i)^2 + \frac{1}{2} \left( \mu_i - \hat{\sigma}(a(x_1 - x_2)) \right)^2 \right) \]

Using the known values:
\[ \sum_{i=1}^{2} (x_i - \mu_i)^2 = \frac{1}{2} \left( \sum_{i=1}^{2} (x_i - \mu_i)^2 + \frac{1}{2} \left( \mu_i - \frac{1}{2} \hat{\sigma}(a(x_1 - x_2)) \right)^2 \right) \]

