\[ u = \frac{\cos x}{1 + \tan x}, \quad dv = \frac{\sin x}{(1 + \tan x)^2} \, dx \]

Then,
\[ I = \left[ \frac{du}{v} \right]_{0}^{\frac{\pi}{2}} - \int_{0}^{\frac{\pi}{2}} \frac{\sin x}{(1 + \tan x)^2} \, dx. \]

### Substituting and Calculating:
\[ \int_{0}^{\frac{\pi}{2}} \frac{\cos x}{1 + \tan x} \, dx = \left[ \frac{(-\cos x)}{1 + \tan x} - \int_{0}^{\frac{\pi}{2}} \frac{\sin x}{(1 + \tan x)^2} \, dx \right]. \]

### Applying Power Rule:
\[ \int_{0}^{\frac{\pi}{2}} \frac{\sin x}{1 + \tan x} \, dx = \left[ \ln |1 + \tan x| - \int_{0}^{\frac{\pi}{2}} \frac{\sin x}{(1 + \tan x)^3} \, dx \right]. \]

### Simplification:
\[ \int_{0}^{\frac{\pi}{2}} \frac{\sin x}{1 + \tan x} \, dx = \left[ \ln |1 + \tan x| - \int_{0}^{\frac{\pi}{2}} \frac{\sin x}{(1 + \tan x)^3} \, dx \right]. \]

By applying the power rule again:
\[ \int_{0}^{\frac{\pi}{2}} \frac{\sin x}{1 + \tan x} \, dx = \left[ \ln |1 + \tan x| - \int_{0}^{\frac{\pi}{2}} \frac{\sin x}{(1 + \tan x)^3} \, dx \right]_{0}^{\frac{\pi}{2}}. \]

Finally, substitute:
\[ \boxed{\ln |1 + \tan x| - \int_{0}^{\frac{\pi}{2}} \frac{\sin x}{(1 + \tan x)^3} \, dx} \]

This completes the solution for \( I \).<|im_end|>
