Next, consider the ratio:
\[ \frac{\sin^2{(a \pi)x} + \sin^2{(a \pi)y}}{a^2} \]

By comparing this to \( \frac{\sin^2{(a \pi)x} - \sin^2{(a \pi)y}}{a^2} \), both ratios have the same sign:
\[ \sin^2{(a \pi)x} - \sin^2{(a \pi)y} < 0 \]

Therefore, the inequality simplifies to:
\[ \sin^2{(a \pi)x} - \sin^2{(a \pi)y} < 0 \]

To find the maximum value, consider the range:
\[ | \sin^2{(a \pi)x} - \sin^2{(a \pi)y}| = |\sin^2{(a \pi)x} - \sin^2{(a \pi)y}| \leq |a| \cdot \sqrt{1 - \cos^2{(a \pi)}} \]

