Question: **Translation of the Vietnamese math problem to English:**

For any positive integer \( n \), define \( \sigma(n) \) as the sum of all divisors of \( n \). Determine:
\[ \lim_{n \to \infty} \frac{\sigma(n^{2023})}{\sigma(n)} \]

**Note:** If \( \sigma(n) \) is non-negative for all \( n \), then \( \lim_{n \to \infty} \sigma(n) = +\infty \); otherwise, \( \lim_{n \to \infty} \sigma(n) \) is the smallest constant \( C \) such that for every real number \( K > C \), there exists a natural number \( N \) such that \( a_n < K \) with \( n > N \).

**Solution:**
Given \( \sigma(n) = \sum_{d|n} d \):
\[ \lim_{n \to \infty} \frac{\sigma(n^{2023})}{\sigma(n)} = \lim_{n \to \infty} \left( \frac{\sum_{d|n} d^n}{\sum_{d|n} d} \right) \]
Since \( \sum_{d|n} d^n = (1+2+\cdots+n)^n \),
\[ \lim_{n \to \infty} \frac{\sigma(n^{2023})}{\sigma(n)} = \lim_{n \to \infty} \left( \frac{(1+2+\cdots+n)^{2023}}{n} \right) \]
This simplifies to:
\[ \lim_{n \to \infty} \frac{(2024!)}{n} \]
Thus,
\[ \boxed{\lim_{n \to \infty} \frac{(2024!)}{n}} = 2024! \]

This completes the solution.
