Given \( n \) students per class with a height distribution among them, each group of \( 3n \) students is unique within their classes. Divide these groups into three groups (each containing one student from each class). Let's denote the highest student in each group as "H". Assume that any possible division of students results in at least 10 students having heights greater than or equal to H. Find the minimum value of \( n \).

**Solution:**

Let’s define:
- \( n \): number of students per class,
- \( h_i \): height of the \( i^\text{th} \) student for all \( i = 1, 2, \ldots, n \),
- \( G \): total number of students divided into groups of 3,

