1. Each group has \( 3n \) students.
2. The heights of all \( 3n \) students differ uniquely between classes.
3. At least 10 students have heights greater than or equal to \( h_1 \).
4. Any group division results in at least 10 students exceeding \( h_1 \).

From these conditions, we deduce:
\[ 3n > 10 \]
\[ 3n - 10 < 3n \]

Solving these inequalities:
\[ 3n - 10 < 3n \implies -10 < 0 \implies n \geq 5 \]

Thus, **the minimum value of \( n \)** is:
\[
\boxed{5}
\]
