- \(5 \text{ rows} \times 20 \text{ red cells per row} = 100 \) red cells.
- \(6 \text{ columns} \times 24 \text{ blue cells per column} = 144 \) blue cells.

The total number of cells is:
\[ 100 + 144 = 244 \]

Thus, the condition ensures:
\[ M = 244 \]

