\]

Next, use the LCM formula:
\[
\text{LCM}(A_1, A_2) = \frac{\text{GCD}(A_1, A_2)}{\text{GCD}(A_1, A_2)}
\]
Substitute \( \text{GCD}(A_1, A_2) = 2014 \):
\[
\text{LCM}(A_1, A_2) = \frac{2014}{2014} = 1
\]

Thus, \( A_1 \cup A_2 \) contains exactly \( 2015 \) distinct numbers because:
\[
\text{LCM}(A_1, A_2) = 2015
\]

Therefore, \( n = 37 \) is the smallest integer required:

**\( n = 37 \)**

