For all real numbers \( x \), compute the limit:

\[ g(x) = \lim_{r \to 0} \left( (x + 1)^{r+1} - x^{r+1} \right)^{\frac{1}{r}} \]

Find \(\lim_{x \to \infty} \frac{g(x)}{x}\).

**Answer:**  
\[ \boxed{\lim_{x \to \infty} \frac{g(x)}{x} = 1} \]
Gold: $e$
