**Answer:**
\[ \boxed{\lim_{R \to \infty} I(R)} = 0 \]

This is derived from the definition of the surface integral over a region bounded by \( x^2 + y^2 \leq R^2 \). The limits approach infinity for \( R \rightarrow \infty \).
