\[
\sum_{k=1}^\infty (-1)^{k-1} \frac{A(k)}{k}
\]

where \( A(k) = \text{number of non-negative divisors of } k \mod [1, \sqrt{k}] \). 

**Note:** This sum is evaluated over all \( k \) from 1 up to \( \sqrt{k} \). The result will be a series expansion involving \( -1 \) raised to powers of \( k \).
