Given a vocabulary encoding with size \( |V| = 99 \), compute the weight function \( a(w) \) for each input sequence \( w = (w_1, ..., w_{99}) \). The weight is defined as:
\[ a(w) = \frac{(n + 1 - \text{count of unique tokens})^{-1}}{n}. \]

Calculate \( \sum_{w \in V^{99}} a(w) \).

**Answer:** 
\[ \boxed{\sum_{w \in V^{99}} a(w)} = \frac{(99 + 1 - n)^{-1}}{99} \]

This gives us the weighted sum over all sequences in the vocabulary space.
