\[ f_2(n) \circ tr_2(\sigma_1^{-3}) = f_2(n) \cdot tr_2(\sigma_1^{-3}) \]

Using the properties of trace and modular inverse:

\[ tr_2(\sigma_1^{-3}) = \text{trace}_{\text{mod}} \left( \frac{\sigma_1}{\sigma_1^{-3}} \right). \]

Thus,

\[ f_2(n) \circ tr_2(\sigma_1^{-3}) = f_2(n) \cdot \text{trace}_{\text{mod}} \left( \frac{\sigma_1}{\sigma_1^{-3}} \right) = f_2(n) \cdot \text{trace}_n \left( \frac{\sigma_1}{\sigma_1^{-3}} \right). \]

