\[ D(\alpha) = \frac{d}{d\alpha} (1 - \frac{1}{\alpha} + \frac{\alpha^3}{6!}) = \frac{-\alpha^2}{6!} - \frac{\alpha^4}{7!} + O(\alpha^5). \]

Since \(D(\alpha)\) tends to zero as \(|\alpha| \to \infty\), the condition \(A(\alpha) = 0\) holds true for all \(|\alpha|\leq 1\).

