Given a cube with edge length \( s \), let \( P \) be one of its vertices, and \( D = \{ (x, y, z) \mid x < s, y < s, z < s \} \) where \( x, y, z \in [0, 1] \). Calculate \( \frac{\text{Area}(D)}{\text{Area}(S)} \).

